{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>A voice.</b> Joined to the glory of HaShem, for the word of HaShem endures alone, not like a human being's, and the sense of <b>a voice says, call</b> is the angel who says to the prophet, call:" "<b>All flesh is grass.</b> Like grass, as in <b>כי שמש ומגן יי</b> (Psalms 84:12):" "<b>Like the flower of the field.</b> In the morning it flowers and passes; by evening it withers and dries (Psalms 90:6)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:03.800534464Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}